WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.857
Word order can change meaning even when the vocabulary barely changes.

00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:12.192
Compare “the dog chased the cat” with “the cat chased the dog.” A Bag-of-Words representation mainly records

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:19.362
which words appear and how often, so these two sentences can look extremely similar in feature space.

00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:21.937
But the grammatical roles are reversed.

00:00:21.937 --> 00:00:25.537
One animal is the agent and the other is the object.

00:00:25.537 --> 00:00:31.162
Transformers process an ordered sequence of tokens, include position information,

00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:33.747
and let tokens interact through attention.

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:40.552
That gives the model a way to represent who is related to whom and how those relationships depend

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:46.622
on order. Bag-of-Words is not wrong; it is simply designed for a different level of representation.

00:00:46.622 --> 00:00:50.032
For many tasks it is still a strong baseline.

00:00:50.032 --> 00:00:55.897
Transformers become useful when context, order, and relationships among tokens carry information that simple

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:58.908
counts cannot capture.
